// firestore.rules — reference copy of the Firestore Security Rules this
// project's global leaderboard depends on.
//
// This file is NOT deployed automatically. This repo is a static site with
// no backend and no Firebase CLI / deploy workflow (see AGENTS.md /
// README.md) — nothing reads this file at build or run time. It exists so
// the rules actually protecting the live database have a version-controlled
// source of truth that reviewers and future edits can diff against, instead
// of living only in the Firebase Console with no history.
//
// To publish a change: paste this file's contents into
// Firebase Console → Firestore Database → Rules → Publish.
//
// Keep this file, the SETUP INSTRUCTIONS comment at the top of
// js/utils/firebase.js, and the numeric bounds in that file's
// clampWireNumber() calls all in sync with whatever is actually deployed —
// a mismatch either clamps away real precision (client bound tighter than
// the rule) or silently loses submissions to a rule the client never
// learns about (client bound looser than the rule).
//
// avgPopularity/fansM: 0-1000 / 0-2200. Widened from an original 0-100 /
// 0-50 after the player-popularity data ceiling was raised (140 -> 350),
// which pushed a real star-chasing roster's avgPopularity/fansM past the
// original bounds and caused the great majority of global submissions to
// be rejected outright.
//
// timestampMs: intentionally NOT compared against request.time. It is
// client-reported (Date.now()), and comparing it to Firestore's server
// clock (e.g. `timestampMs <= request.time.toMillis() + 60000`) rejects
// every write from a device whose clock reads meaningfully ahead of
// Firestore's — a common, entirely legitimate condition (unsynced system
// clock, wrong timezone, clock drift) that fails with the exact same
// generic PERMISSION_DENIED as every other cause. Do not add that
// comparison back. Time-window reads (24h/weekly) instead filter on the
// `timestamp` field, which Firestore stamps server-side via
// serverTimestamp() and is authoritative regardless of the client's clock.
//
// users/{uid}: the per-player cloud save behind the optional account system.
// The block existed here unused for a long time as a bare owner-only
// read/write; it now also validates the document's shape and bounds every
// string and array, per the accounts plan. Two deliberate restraints, both
// following the avgPopularity lesson above rather than repeating it:
//
//   * It bounds SIZE and STRUCTURE, never values. A user document is
//     readable and writable only by its owner, so the worst a bad write can
//     do is corrupt that one player's own save — while a rule tighter than
//     what the game legitimately produces would reject real saves from
//     everyone, silently and with the same generic PERMISSION_DENIED.
//   * Every numeric check is `is number`, never `is int`. Whether the
//     Firestore Web SDK sends a plain JS number as an integer or a double is
//     not a thing to bet a player's progress on.
//
// The array caps (leaderboard 20, trophies 12, mode boards 20) mirror the
// writers in js/utils/storage.js and the merge in js/utils/cloudSave.js, so
// those three MUST be changed together — a cap raised in the game but not
// here rejects the first save that exceeds it. legends is bounded at 2000
// against a 937-player database: headroom for the data to grow, deliberately
// loose for the same reason avgPopularity is.
//
// dailyLeaderboard score: asserted EQUAL to wins * 10 + (passed ? 200 : 0),
// not merely bounded. This is the one place in either public collection where
// a submitted number can be checked against the rest of its own document
// instead of taken on trust, and `score` is the board's primary sort key — a
// bare range let anything inside it top the day outright. The formula is
// dailyScore() in js/logic/challenge.js, mirrored by buildDailyDoc() in
// js/utils/firebase.js (which recomputes rather than forwards `score`, so no
// legitimate submission can miss this) and re-checked on read by
// fetchDailyLeaderboard() for documents written before the rule. It is also
// the rule the setup-instructions comment at the top of js/utils/firebase.js
// has always documented — this file had drifted to `score >= 0 && <= 2000`,
// which is the looser of the two and was NOT what that comment described.
//
// This does not make the boards forgery-proof, and cannot: anyone holding the
// public web config can write a document, so every rule here bounds what a
// forgery may CLAIM rather than proving a run happened. Doing better needs a
// server to sign results, which this project deliberately does not have.
//
// uid on leaderboard/dailyLeaderboard: optional, and when present must equal
// the writer's own auth uid. Anonymous submissions omit it entirely and are
// completely unaffected — they remain the overwhelming majority and must
// keep working byte-for-byte. Note this only ever TIGHTENS: neither rule used
// hasOnly(), so before this clause a forged `uid` would have been accepted
// without any check at all.
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    // A signed-in player may stamp their own uid onto a public leaderboard
    // document; nobody may stamp anyone else's. Anonymous submissions omit
    // the field entirely and are unaffected — which is the whole point, as
    // they are still the overwhelming majority. Before this clause a `uid`
    // field would have been accepted unvalidated, so this only tightens.
    function optionalOwnUid() {
      return !('uid' in request.resource.data)
             || (request.resource.data.uid is string
                 && request.auth != null
                 && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid);
    }

    function isOwner(uid) {
      return request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
    }

    // Caps mirror the writers in js/utils/storage.js and the merge in
    // js/utils/cloudSave.js: leaderboard 20, trophies 12, each mode board
    // 20. A merged save can never exceed them, so a document that does was
    // not written by this game.
    //
    // legends has no cap in the game — it grows by one per player id ever
    // drafted — so 2000 is generous headroom over the 937 players the
    // shipped database currently holds. Same approach as the
    // avgPopularity/fansM bounds above, and for the same reason: leave room
    // for the data to grow rather than re-cut the rule every time it does.
    // Accessed with map.get(key, default) rather than dot or bracket notation:
    // two of these keys contain a hyphen, so m.gm-ai would parse as
    // subtraction, and get() is the documented Map accessor. The `in` guard
    // still runs first so an absent board is simply absent, not an empty one.
    function modeBoardsValid(m) {
      return m.keys().hasOnly(['defense', 'fans', 'gm-ai', 'dynasty-duel'])
             && (!('defense'      in m) || (m.get('defense', [])      is list && m.get('defense', []).size()      <= 20))
             && (!('fans'         in m) || (m.get('fans', [])         is list && m.get('fans', []).size()         <= 20))
             && (!('gm-ai'        in m) || (m.get('gm-ai', [])        is list && m.get('gm-ai', []).size()        <= 20))
             && (!('dynasty-duel' in m) || (m.get('dynasty-duel', []) is list && m.get('dynasty-duel', []).size() <= 20));
    }

    function saveValid(s) {
      return s.keys().hasOnly(['progress', 'legends', 'leaderboard', 'trophies',
                               'modeBoards', 'daily', 'dynastyDuel', 'bests'])
             && (!('progress'    in s) || s.progress is map)
             && (!('legends'     in s) || (s.legends     is list && s.legends.size()     <= 2000))
             && (!('leaderboard' in s) || (s.leaderboard is list && s.leaderboard.size() <= 20))
             && (!('trophies'    in s) || (s.trophies    is list && s.trophies.size()    <= 12))
             && (!('modeBoards'  in s) || (s.modeBoards  is map  && modeBoardsValid(s.modeBoards)))
             && (!('daily'       in s) || s.daily       is map)
             && (!('dynastyDuel' in s) || s.dynastyDuel is map)
             && (!('bests'       in s) || s.bests       is map);
    }

    // Every numeric field is checked with `is number`, never `is int`: the
    // Firestore Web SDK's choice between an integer and a double for a
    // plain JS number is not something this rule should be betting a
    // player's save on.
    function userDocValid(d) {
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['displayName', 'schemaVersion', 'createdAt',
                               'updatedAt', 'deviceUpdatedAt', 'save'])
             && (!('displayName' in d) || (d.displayName is string
                                           && d.displayName.size() >= 3
                                           && d.displayName.size() <= 24))
             && (!('schemaVersion'   in d) || (d.schemaVersion is number
                                               && d.schemaVersion >= 1
                                               && d.schemaVersion <= 1000))
             && (!('deviceUpdatedAt' in d) || d.deviceUpdatedAt is number)
             && (!('createdAt'       in d) || d.createdAt is timestamp)
             && (!('updatedAt'       in d) || d.updatedAt is timestamp)
             && (!('save'            in d) || (d.save is map && saveValid(d.save)));
    }

    match /leaderboard/{docId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if request.resource.data.wins is number
                    && request.resource.data.wins >= 0
                    && request.resource.data.wins <= 82
                    && request.resource.data.losses is number
                    && request.resource.data.losses >= 0
                    && request.resource.data.losses <= 82
                    && request.resource.data.teamName is string
                    && request.resource.data.teamName.size() <= 30
                    && request.resource.data.coachId is string
                    && request.resource.data.coachId.size() <= 20
                    && request.resource.data.coachName is string
                    && request.resource.data.coachName.size() <= 30
                    && request.resource.data.era is string
                    && request.resource.data.era.size() <= 10
                    && request.resource.data.starters is string
                    && request.resource.data.starters.size() <= 100
                    && request.resource.data.chemScore is number
                    && request.resource.data.chemScore >= 0
                    && request.resource.data.chemScore <= 100
                    && (!('avgPopularity' in request.resource.data)
                        || (request.resource.data.avgPopularity is number
                            && request.resource.data.avgPopularity >= 0
                            && request.resource.data.avgPopularity <= 1000))
                    && (!('fansM' in request.resource.data)
                        || (request.resource.data.fansM is number
                            && request.resource.data.fansM >= 0
                            && request.resource.data.fansM <= 2200))
                    && request.resource.data.champion is bool
                    && request.resource.data.timestampMs is number
                    && optionalOwnUid();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    match /dailyLeaderboard/{docId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if request.resource.data.date is string
                    && request.resource.data.date.size() == 10
                    && request.resource.data.wins is number
                    && request.resource.data.wins >= 0
                    && request.resource.data.wins <= 82
                    && request.resource.data.losses is number
                    && request.resource.data.losses >= 0
                    && request.resource.data.losses <= 82
                    && request.resource.data.teamName is string
                    && request.resource.data.teamName.size() <= 30
                    && request.resource.data.coachId is string
                    && request.resource.data.coachId.size() <= 20
                    && request.resource.data.coachName is string
                    && request.resource.data.coachName.size() <= 30
                    && request.resource.data.chemScore is number
                    && request.resource.data.chemScore >= 0
                    && request.resource.data.chemScore <= 100
                    && request.resource.data.starters is string
                    && request.resource.data.starters.size() <= 100
                    && request.resource.data.champion is bool
                    && request.resource.data.timestampMs is number
                    && request.resource.data.challengeId is string
                    && request.resource.data.challengeId.size() <= 40
                    && request.resource.data.passed is bool
                    && request.resource.data.score is number
                    && request.resource.data.score ==
                         request.resource.data.wins * 10
                         + (request.resource.data.passed ? 200 : 0)
                    && optionalOwnUid();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ── Per-player cloud save ────────────────────────────────────────────
    // One document per authenticated user, mirroring the nba820_* local
    // keys (see js/utils/cloudSave.js for the snapshot shape it writes).
    //
    // The threat model here is much weaker than the two public collections
    // above: a document is readable and writable ONLY by the account that
    // owns it, so nobody can forge someone else's save. What is left to
    // defend against is a client bug and the use of a user document as
    // free unbounded storage — so these rules bound structure and size,
    // and deliberately do NOT police values.
    //
    // That restraint is the lesson this file already records at the top:
    // rules tighter than what the game legitimately produces reject real
    // writes and fail with the same generic PERMISSION_DENIED as a dozen
    // unrelated causes. A save whose xp is "wrong" costs one player their
    // own numbers; a rule that rejects valid saves costs every player
    // their progress silently.

    match /users/{uid} {
      // Not publicly readable. If a public profile is ever wanted it belongs
      // in a separate document holding only the fields meant to be public,
      // never by loosening this one.
      allow read:          if isOwner(uid);
      allow create, update: if isOwner(uid) && userDocValid(request.resource.data);
      // Account deletion has to actually erase the data, so the owner — and
      // only the owner — may delete their own document.
      allow delete:        if isOwner(uid);
    }
  }
}
